ORIGINAL REQUEST:
Given Output Metadata on Port 0:
<Metadata id="OutAuditSchedule">
<Record name="AuditScheduleRecord" fieldDelimiter="," recordDelimiter="\n" type="delimited">
    <Field name="control_run_id" type="long"/>
    <Field name="review_date" type="date" format="yyyy-MM-dd"/>
    <Field name="compliance_year" type="integer" nullable="false"/>
    <Field name="compliance_month" type="integer"/>
    <Field name="iso_week_number" type="integer" nullable="true"/>
    <Field name="weekday_code" type="integer"/>
    <Field name="season_window" type="string" nullable="false"/>
    <Field name="site_visit_required" type="boolean"/>
</Record>
</Metadata>

Write a DataGenerator that creates a Nordics energy and utilities compliance audit schedule for dates from 2024-10-01 through 2025-03-31, but only outputs records when the date is either a Monday or the last calendar day of the month. Populate season_window as "dark_season" for dates in November through February and "shoulder_season" otherwise. Set site_visit_required to true only when the generated date is the last calendar day of the month and is not a Saturday or Sunday.

PROPOSED CTL2 IMPLEMENTATION:
```ctl
//#CTL2

date currentDate;
date endDate;

function boolean init() {
    currentDate = str2date("2024-10-01", "yyyy-MM-dd");
    endDate = str2date("2025-03-31", "yyyy-MM-dd");
    return true;
}

function integer generate() {
    if (currentDate > endDate) {
        return STOP;
    }

    integer dayOfWeek = getDayOfWeek(currentDate);
    integer dayOfMonth = getDay(currentDate);
    integer month = getMonth(currentDate);
    integer year = getYear(currentDate);

    // Check if it's Monday or last day of the month
    boolean isMonday = (dayOfWeek == 2);
    boolean isLastDayOfMonth = (dateAdd(currentDate, 1, day) > dateAdd(currentDate, -1, month));

    if (!isMonday && !isLastDayOfMonth) {
        currentDate = dateAdd(currentDate, 1, day);
        return SKIP;
    }

    $out.0.control_run_id = randomLong();
    $out.0.review_date = currentDate;
    $out.0.compliance_year = year;
    $out.0.compliance_month = month;
    $out.0.iso_week_number = getWeekNumber(currentDate);
    $out.0.weekday_code = dayOfWeek;

    if (month >= 11 || month <= 2) {
        $out.0.season_window = "dark_season";
    } else {
        $out.0.season_window = "shoulder_season";
    }

    // Site visit required only on last day of month and not weekend
    $out.0.site_visit_required = isLastDayOfMonth && (dayOfWeek != 6 && dayOfWeek != 7);

    currentDate = dateAdd(currentDate, 1, day);
    return OK;
}
```
